<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RSW_Filth_WhaleDung.xml   SWBestiary — FILTH_ON_NATURAL_TERRAIN_NOOP_1

  Fixes a shipped no-op: RSW_ShadeWhale's RM_CompDungSeeder and
  RM_JobDriver_FilterFeedTerrain both dropped Core's Filth_AnimalFilth,
  whose <filth><placementMask> is [Terrain]-only
  (Data/Core/ThingDefs_Misc/Filth_Various.xml). Every terrain deriving
  NaturalTerrainBase — Sand, SoftSand, all of it — declares
  filthAcceptanceMask [Unnatural]-only (Data/Core/TerrainDefs/
  Terrain_Natural.xml), and FilthMaker.TerrainAcceptsFilth requires the
  filth's mask to be a SUBSET of the terrain's, so [Terrain] against
  [Unnatural]-only is false unconditionally. Confirmed live 2026-09-21:
  six filter-feed bouts and eight dung events on open Sand, 0 filth.

  🔴 The forbidden fix is patching Sand/SoftSand's own filthAcceptanceMask
  — both are Core TerrainDefs and CLAUDE.md bars touching a Core
  TerrainDef's mask to make our own content visible.

  The fix that IS available: RimWorld/FilthProperties.cs's own C# default
  for an unset <placementMask> is FilthSourceFlags.Unnatural, not
  [Terrain] — which is exactly what NaturalTerrainBase accepts. That is
  why Filth_Blood/Filth_Vomit/Filth_Water/etc. (none of which declare
  <placementMask> in Core's own Filth_Various.xml) already show up on
  ordinary grass and dirt outdoors, while Filth_Dirt/Filth_Sand/
  Filth_AnimalFilth/Filth_Trash — every Core filth that explicitly sets
  [Terrain] — do not. This def follows that same precedent deliberately
  (declared here rather than left to the default, so the intent survives
  a reader who does not already know FilthProperties' default): a
  whale-dung filth carrying [Unnatural] only, which Sand/SoftSand's
  [Unnatural] acceptance mask accepts outright — no roof, no enclosed
  room, no FilthSourceFlags.Pawn escape hatch needed (that hatch, per
  RimWorld/FilthMaker.cs's own CanMakeFilth, only ever unlocks the
  roofed/enclosed case, confirmed against the decompile; open desert sand
  never qualifies).

  Same visual as Filth_AnimalFilth (Core's own dung tint over the same
  grainy-cluster look) — this def changes ONLY the placement mask, not the
  look. RSW_ShadeWhale.xml wires this in as both dungFilthDef and
  leavingsFilthDef in place of Filth_AnimalFilth.

  texPath: this mod ships its own Textures/Things/ namespace, so
  validate_patch.py refuses a bare cross-mod reference to Core's own
  Things/Filth/Grainy as an unresolvable texPath (same rule that hit
  RimUtinni's RUT_Filth_MouseTrack). Not a DEPLOY_HOLD placeholder this
  time — the actual Core GrainyA texture (extracted via
  extract_bundle_textures.py, cached at
  observed/inventory/bundle_textures/ludeon.rimworld.core/GrainyA.png) is
  copied in at Textures/Things/Filth/RSW_WhaleDung.png, so this renders
  real Core art under this mod's own path rather than a magenta square.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseFilth">
    <defName>RSW_Filth_WhaleDung</defName>
    <label>whale dung</label>
    <description>A massive deposit left by a shade whale — the megafauna's own fertiliser, and the visible mark of where it stopped.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Filth/RSW_WhaleDung</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <color>(97,65,48,97)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <filth>
      <placementMask>
        <li>Unnatural</li>
      </placementMask>
      <rainWashes>true</rainWashes>
      <disappearsInDays>45~50</disappearsInDays>
      <cleaningWorkToReduceThickness>35</cleaningWorkToReduceThickness>
      <canFilthAttach>true</canFilthAttach>
    </filth>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
